Z||000000||Hank is Here||04-22-2001||07:19 PM||||Alright... I think I have a clogged cat tell me what you guys think.  <P>1) runs HOT at idle<BR>2) car is hard to start, seems like it is choking  <BR>3) has limited upper end acceleration, compared to an 86 GT auto <BR>4) fuel mileage has been decreasing was 24 mpg highway not 22mpg  <P>Do you all think it is time for a new cat?<BR>Also any recommendations as to good cats? The only one I know of is Rodney's one.  What do you guys think of his cat?  <P>Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000001||MooCow||04-22-2001||08:29 PM||||Hit the cat and see if it makes a noise.  You should hear things when you hit like metalinside of it.  If it makes noise when you hit it then I believe that means it is shot.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||04-22-2001||09:00 PM||||  Hank, I have been experiencing the same symptoms. My car will run a little hot at a stop light, it has very limited power compare to what it used to have and the gas milage has dropped almost three mile to the gallon over the past six months. As far as starting, it will start right up then die after about three seconds. This will happen a couple of times and then she stays lit. I also had a close call at smog busters when I went to re-register my car. LMK know what you think. I have been thinking it's the cat, but the engine swap is just around the corner. I will probably get Chris Wests free flow cat. <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/</A> <P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||12
Z||000003||Mi Junk||04-22-2001||10:56 PM||||Not to scare you guys, but on my 85 GT the contents of the cat were in the muffler. So needless to say the cat was empty and the muffler was plugged.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000004||Tom88gt||04-23-2001||09:14 AM||||The catalyst should just ceramic.  If it's breaking apart, I would think that it will rattle and make lots of noise until it pulverizes itself to dust and is blown out the tailpipe.  May take a while.  <P>I once knocked out the ceramic stuff on a Jeep and it just broke into small pieces and then to dust as I hit it.  The Jeep had 120,000 miles on it and I could still see light through the element (but I don't know what it looked like new).  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hank is Here||04-23-2001||04:40 PM||||I think it is my cat now.  Always since I have had the car (about 1 year) it did rattle when I closed the door or even when at low idle.  I haven't put many miles on the car only like 8k or so.  Of late the problem is more apparent so new cat time. The car now has a little over 130,000 and I guess things are starting to go. <P>BAM your problems sound exactly like mine<P>Hank is Here (Mark)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||ToddAsh||04-23-2001||08:55 PM|||| I just replaced the cat on my daughter's Cherokee because it had the exact same symptons as yours. Just took the cat off my '85 V6 SE.What a difference. I don't know if it was clogged or what but the car only has 16,000 miles and it runs awsome now.One of our popular Fiero vendors told me removing the cat was the best performance modification I could make.Well,it's a little loud but it sure gets up quick. Todd||||reg||1
Z||000007||skitime||04-23-2001||09:24 PM||||All three of the Fieros we have now had clogged cats. One rattling brick, one loose brick, and one not letting hardly anything through with exhaust leaks everywhere. So what are the chances yours is clogged. My guess near 100%.  We only replaced the first one with a Rodney Dickman cat. After that we replaced them with a Cherry Bomb muffler (much cheaper and quieter than the cat.)||||reg||1
